{
  "message": "The references don’t establish a playable core, a common gap you can address this checkpoint. Mia has joined, but her unstated hours mean the plan cannot depend on her coding time. Before approving, narrow the goal and replace the trailer storyboard with the three prototype tasks below. We’ll review after the first sprint; I look forward to your build and devlog posts ;).",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvtjvqem07clnxz8pdhgkj7t",
      "kind": "cut",
      "note": "Drop the trailer storyboard: it uses time needed to test sailing and the tide loop.",
      "suggestion": null
    }
  ],
  "add": [
    "Sprint 1: Make a rough single-player sailing test with one boat and one island, and share a playable build.",
    "Sprints 2–3: Add one complete tide cycle that changes where the boat can sail, and share a playable build.",
    "Sprint 4: Test the build with five players and publish a devlog with the build link, observed problems, and what to change next."
  ],
  "goal": {
    "fit": "narrow",
    "note": "Without a demonstrated core, two islands and co-op are too much for 40–60 confirmed hours. Use: A rough single-player prototype with one island and a tide cycle, tested by five players, with findings published in a devlog."
  }
}

